 },
 "critic": "Interchangeable names, repeated full names, fixed rewards, generic occupations, and identical sentence structures made most cards read as assembled. Repeated families included Friday extortion messages, sealed-case deliveries, accident notices, assault bulletins, and pocket warnings. The extortion cards still had a strong causal chain: recurring gang collection creates a shortage and prompts an appeal. Many other cards named an event without explaining anyone's motive. The pavement image and eyewitness bag theft felt more individually written, though those guesses are tentative."
